{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>The length of the court.</b> The north and the south, from east to west — <b>a hundred cubits.</b>" "<b>And the breadth fifty by fifty.</b> The court on the east was square, fifty by fifty — for the Mishkan, its length thirty and its breadth ten; he placed the east of its opening at the edge of the outer fifty of the length of the court. It is thus all within the inner fifty, and its length terminates at thirty — leaving twenty cubits of space behind it between the hangings on the west and the curtains at the back of the Mishkan. And the breadth of the Mishkan, ten cubits, is in the middle of the breadth of the court — leaving twenty cubits of space to the north and to the south, from the court's hangings to the Mishkan's curtains, and likewise to the west. And fifty by fifty — a court in front of it." "<b>And its height five cubits.</b> The height of the court's partitions — and this is the breadth of the hangings." "<b>And their sockets copper.</b> To include the sockets of the screen — so that you not say: copper sockets were specified only for the pillars of the hangings, but the sockets of the screen were of a different material. Thus it appears to me, that this is why he repeated and stated it."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:01.528449998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}